  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "The top-3 configs (043, 047, 013) all use scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l with multiprofile, and the best (config_043, acc=0.7250) uses transformer aggregation + weighted fusion. The image encoder dimension is completely unexplored with the best RNA/aggregation/fusion settings. config_018 (scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted) tests whether a different visual backbone can match or exceed ViT-L while keeping the proven RNA encoder and fusion strategy. Image-only performance was very low (0.33), so the image branch contributes modestly, but a better/more complementary representation could still push the multimodal accuracy above 0.725. This is the highest-value remaining uncertainty: if resnet50 matches ViT-L, we gain a cheaper pipeline; if it underperforms, we confirm ViT-L is necessary and can focus remaining budget on other refinements. Expected relative cost: lower than config_043 (~2.5–3.0 GPU hrs vs 3.60) since resnet50 is a smaller backbone than ViT-L, making this a cost-efficient exploration of the last major untested architectural axis."
}

